{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mphwiorsu3so6bcjiqqyznzlngqlvmyd4v4e7xwceaxmpxtus3wq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The library**: one translation unit (`c_src/src/lib.c`), one public symbol — `hex2bin` (the libsodium-style branch-free hex decoder).\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (all in the crate root, derived mechanically from the C):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C `.so` exports exactly `hex2bin`; Rust `.so` exports it too. `comm -23` diff is **empty**, 0 non-libc undefined symbols. No C source was left untranslated, so nothing had to be written from scratch.\n- `ERRORS.md` — **20 rows**, one per distinct rejection in the C: `bin_maxlen` exhaustion (2 forms), odd digit count (`state != 0` → `hex_pos--`), strict-mode unconsumed input, the ignore-set guards (`ignore != NULL`, `state == 0`, `strchr` miss), the `strchr(ignore, 0)` NUL quirk, all 256 stop bytes, range-boundary bytes, NULL pointers, oversized lengths.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **33 rows** across the axes the C branches on (`ignore` NULL/empty/multi/hex-containing/high-bit, `hex_end_p` NULL vs set, `bin_maxlen` 0/short/exact/slack/`usize::MAX`, digit case classes, separator placement incl. mid-byte, partial views, in-place aliasing, 4 KiB inputs).\n\n**Phases B/C** — 57 tests in `tests/`, loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and calling only exported symbols. Each case compares return value, the *entire* `bin` allocation (incl. slack past `bin_maxlen`), the `*hex_end_p` offset, and the `hex` buffer afterwards. Coverage includes exhaustive enumeration of all inputs of length ≤ 2 and **all 16.7 M three-byte inputs** — ≈ 35 M comparisons, all byte-identical. Also re-verified with an `-O2` C build vs a `--release` Rust build.\n\n**Phase D** — symbol diff empty (also asserted as a test); `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so there is exactly one combination, driven by `scripts/feature_combos.sh` + `scripts/run_diff_tests.sh`.\n\n**No Rust changes were needed** — the translation already matched, including the `~state` toggle, promotion/truncation chain, the NUL-as-ignorable-char quirk, and keeping partially written bytes while returning `-1`.\n\nTwo testing traps I found and closed (both had produced false PASSes):\n1. `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target, so tests were loading a **stale** `.so`. Fixed by building first in the script *and* a `STALE SHARED OBJECT` freshness guard in the harness.\n2. Mutants that segfault/abort never print libtest's summary line, so grepping for `test result: FAILED` missed them; detection now uses the exit status.\n\nHarness power was proven by mutation testing (`scripts/mutation_check.py`): **26/26 behaviour-changing mutants detected, 3/3 provably equivalent control mutants correctly not detected (29/29 as expected)**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":159029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50d36bc7-360c-4640-8993-4d9186dc09e4","uuid":"578d3c8a-70a8-4787-b4c0-976cb3127a08","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:00:27.224Z"}
